{
    "_comment": [
        "Frontend-local settings schema. Deliberately the SAME shape as the schema the",
        "backend serves over CONFIG_SCHEMA (0x91), so SettingsView renders local and",
        "remote settings through one delegate family and adding a setting is one entry",
        "here plus one binding in app/Theme.qml.",
        "",
        "TWO LEVELS: groups render as sidebar sections, and each group holds SUBSECTIONS",
        "that render as one card each in the detail pane.",
        "",
        "THIS FILE IS THE CANONICAL SECTION LIST. A group id present here and in the",
        "backend's schema MERGES - 'general' shows the screensaver card below plus the",
        "backend's location card - and this file decides the order, label and icon. That",
        "is why 'media' and 'tesla' appear with no subsections of their own: they hold no",
        "frontend settings, and the entries exist only to place and name them. A backend",
        "group whose id is unknown here is appended rather than dropped, and a section",
        "that ends up with no subsections at all is hidden.",
        "",
        "Per-group keys: id, label, icon (a semantic name mapped to a resource by",
        "SettingsSidebar, not a file path), sections.",
        "",
        "Per-subsection keys: id, label, help (optional, under the card title),\nstatus (optional: names a runtime status widget rendered in the card -\n'backendProbe' is the reachability check), settings.",
        "",
        "Per-setting keys: key, type (bool|int|float|string|enum|action), label, help,",
        "unit, min/max/step (numeric), options\n(enum), default, apply, editor,\nwarnBelow/warnAbove + warnMessage (advisory caution, never blocks a write),\nrelevantWhen {key, equals|notEquals} or {condition} (a runtime fact named in\nSettingRow.conditionHolds), or a list of such rules that must ALL hold\n(fades and disables the row while they do not).",
        "editor: a per-type CONTROL HINT, always opt-in, ignored when absent.",
        "        'slider' (int/float) replaces the default [-] value [+] stepper,",
        "        and only for coarse dials where the exact number does not matter",
        "        (a 65534-step slider is unusable, see SettingNumber).",
        "        'time' (int) renders minutes since midnight as HH:MM on the same",
        "        stepper, wrapping past midnight, with no typing. Use min 0,",
        "        max 1440 - step.",
        "",
        "secret: true (string) masks the value while the field is not being",
        "        edited and keeps it out of the log line a write produces.",
        "",
        "hidden: true keeps a setting out of the rendered rows while still",
        "        storing, coercing and persisting it normally. For a setting whose",
        "        editor lives inside the subsection's status widget - the update",
        "        channel belongs above the verdict it decides, not in a row under",
        "        it - and readable as always through Settings.values / valueOf().",
        "",
        "type 'action' is a BUTTON, not a value: nothing is stored or persisted.",
        "It carries actionLabel and optionally requiresConnection, and its key names",
        "a handler in Settings::invokeAction.",
        "",
        "apply: 'live'    - a QML binding through Theme picks it up immediately;",
        "       'restart' - consumed once at startup (AppConfig), so it needs an app",
        "                   restart. The view badges these rows.",
        "",
        "A setting may also declare 'env': the named environment variable (or .env",
        "entry) supplies that setting's DEFAULT, so an existing deployment keeps",
        "working until the user overrides it here. Precedence: schema default <",
        "env/.env < saved user override.",
        "",
        "Values the user changes are written to frontend_config.json under",
        "~/.config/Tesla-Homedash/ (see core/settings.cpp) - never back into this bundled",
        "file, which is compiled into the binary and supplies only the defaults."
    ],
